adhesions, which often require subsequent intervention. Bioabsorbable, steroid‐eluting sinus stents are inserted into   
the nose, sinuses or both following surgery to prevent stenosis of the sinus openings during the postoperative healing  
period. The slow release of corticosteroid aims to decrease mucosal oedema and expedite wound healing. Whether a        
steroid‐eluting stent offers any beneficial effects in terms of improving sinonasal symptoms has not been systematically
reviewed.", "selection_criteria": "We included all randomised controlled trials (RCTs) comparing steroid‐eluting sinus  
