of chronic sinusitis were evaluated. In randomized fashion, the gel dressing was placed into one operated cavity while  
the contralateral side served as the control. The results indicated that hylan gel was effective in stilling            
postsurgical bleeding, particularly in the fulminant polyposis cases who had a larger and more exposed cavity. These    
early results indicate a potential benefit of a gel dressing for hemostasis when used at the conclusion of the operative
procedure. In addition, other parameters were evaluated in this study, including prevention of postoperative adhesions  
and the effect on mucosal healing. These parameters showed a positive result compared with the control                  
group.search.ebscohost.com"}, {"study_index": 24, "title": "The effect of an absorbable gelatin dressing impregnated    
